            <div xml:id="d1023">

                <pb facs="0900" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">892.6363/69</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">the Chargé in Siam</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chapman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 537</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-02">June 2, 1937</date>.<lb/>[Received June
                        15.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    No. 528 of May 19, 1937,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d1023-f1"/> as well as previous
                    telegrams and despatches, with reference to purported oil control legislation in
                    Siam, and to report that during the course of a conversation yesterday, the
                    Foreign Minister, Luang Pradist Manudharm, denied categorically that an oil
                    control law has been drafted or considered by the Siamese Government.</p>
                <p>I have no reason to doubt the Minister’s word, but I nevertheless cannot escape
                    the impression that the subject is receiving consideration in interested
                    government circles.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Holbrook
                    Chapman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
